# `dfo::DfoProblem`

The data of a derivative-free problem: start, objective or black box, constraints and bounds.

Fill in `initial` and exactly one of `objective` or `blackbox`. `constraints` returns inequality values `g(x) ≤ 0`; `constraints_values` returns both kinds through [`DfoConstraintValues`](DfoConstraintValues.md); give at most one of the two. `lower_bounds` and `upper_bounds` come together and have one element per variable. The problem is checked when it is solved, with an error that names the missing or conflicting part.

Which methods honour what: Nelder-Mead supports bounds (by projection) but no nonlinear constraints; pattern search and the MADS kinds support bounds and nonlinear constraints; the evolutionary and swarm methods support bounds and use them as the sampling box, and reject nonlinear constraints rather than ignore them.

## Fields

### `initial`

`pluss::Series`, default `undefined`.

The starting point; fixes the number of variables.

### `objective`

`std::function<pluss::Series(const pluss::Series &)>`, default `empty`.

The scalar objective.

### `constraints`

`std::function<pluss::Series(const pluss::Series &)>`, default `empty`.

Inequality values `g(x) ≤ 0`.

### `constraints_values`

`std::function<dfo::DfoConstraintValues(const pluss::Series &)>`, default `empty`.

Inequality and equality values.

### `blackbox`

`std::function<dfo::BlackboxEvaluation(const pluss::Series &)>`, default `empty`.

An evaluation that returns objectives, constraints and a success flag.

### `lower_bounds`

`pluss::Series`, default `undefined`.

Lower bound per variable; set together with `upper_bounds`.

### `upper_bounds`

`pluss::Series`, default `undefined`.

Upper bound per variable.

## Guidance

Passed to `DFO::solve` or `DFO::run`.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

An objective with bounds. The unconstrained minimum `(3, 3)` is outside the box `[0, 2]²`, so the answer is the corner `(2, 2)`.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const auto f = [](const Series &x) { return (x - 3.0).square().sum(); };   // minimum 0 at (3, 3)

  dfo::DfoProblem problem;
  problem.initial = pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0});
  problem.objective = f;
  problem.lower_bounds = pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0});
  problem.upper_bounds = pluss::series::make({2.0, 2.0});
  const dfo::DfoResult result = dfo::DFO::solve(problem);
  out.writeln("minimizer =", result.minimizer.items<double>(), ", solver =", dfo::to_string(result.selected_solver));
}
```

### Example 2

A constrained problem. The constraint `x₀ + x₁ ≤ 2` moves the answer from `(3, 3)` to `(1, 1)`.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const auto f = [](const Series &x) { return (x - 3.0).square().sum(); };   // minimum 0 at (3, 3)

  dfo::DfoProblem problem;
  problem.initial = pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0});
  problem.objective = f;
  problem.constraints = [](const Series &x) { return x.sum() - 2.0; };
  const dfo::DfoResult result = dfo::DFO::solve(problem);
  out.writeln("minimizer =", result.minimizer.items<double>(), ", solver =", dfo::to_string(result.selected_solver));
}
```

### Example 3

A black box instead of an objective. The callback returns a number; a `BlackboxEvaluation` can also carry constraints and flag a failed evaluation.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const auto f = [](const Series &x) { return (x - 3.0).square().sum(); };   // minimum 0 at (3, 3)

  dfo::DfoProblem problem;
  problem.initial = pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0});
  problem.blackbox = [&](const Series &x) {
    dfo::BlackboxEvaluation e;
    e.objectives = f(x);
    return e;
  };
  const dfo::DfoResult result = dfo::DFO::solve(problem);
  out.writeln("minimizer =", result.minimizer.items<double>(), ", solver =", dfo::to_string(result.selected_solver));
}
```

